# Voice Dictation

A **personal, local "Wispr" for Mac** — a single-user dictation app for the
owner. Hold a global hotkey (e.g. `⌘ + ⌥`), speak, release, and the spoken words
are transcribed and **inserted at the current cursor position** in whatever app
is focused, then also saved to the app's **history**. Fast enough to feel
instant, English-optimized to start.

Each recording is captured to a temporary audio file, transcribed, optionally
run through an **AI cleanup** pass (punctuation, filler removal, formatting),
inserted and logged — and the **audio file is deleted once transcription
succeeds** (only the text is kept). Both the **transcription model** and the
**AI cleanup model/technique** are **selectable in settings**.

Builds directly on the lessons of the `transcriber` project
(`~/dev/transcriber`), whose on-device `mlx-whisper` / `parakeet-mlx` stack is
the biggest proven win so far — this app reuses that approach for the live,
low-latency dictation path rather than starting from scratch.

## Stack (decided at INIT Phase 0 — see the INIT update)
**Native Swift** AppKit menu-bar app (`.accessory`, no Dock icon) for the shell:
global hotkey, menu-bar state, system-wide text insertion. Transcription runs in
a **long-lived Python sidecar** reusing transcriber's on-device MLX path
(`mlx-whisper` / `parakeet-mlx`, Apple Silicon) — Parakeet TDT v3 as the default
fast path — since there's no native Swift ASR here. Optional Groq cloud fast
path and a pluggable AI-cleanup step (none / local / Groq / Claude) layer on top.

## Secrets
- `GROQ_API_KEY` — **optional.** Fast cloud path: Groq `whisper-large-v3-turbo`
  for near-instant transcription and fast LLM cleanup. The on-device default
  needs no secret.
- `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` — **optional.** Higher-quality AI cleanup via Claude,
  selectable as a cleanup model in settings.

Both are optional because the default dictation path runs fully on-device.

